1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,809
Where an adverb stands.

2
00:00:01,809 --> 00:00:09,726
It never comes between a verb and its object: she speaks fluently English is wrong; she speaks English fluently.

3
00:00:09,726 --> 00:00:22,877
Frequency adverbs like always and never go before the main verb, after the verb be, and after the first auxiliary: he always arrives early; he is always late; she has never seen the sea.

4
00:00:22,877 --> 00:00:25,781
And enough comes after: old enough.

